  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Imagined Cosmopolis (2019), published by Peter Lang Verlag, has been cited 1 time.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Imagined Cosmopolis by Charlotte Ashby, Grace Brockington, Daniel Laqua and others was published by Peter Lang Verlag in 2019. It is part of the Internationalism and the Arts series. Conceptually, the work connects to Internationalism (politics), Homeland, The arts, League and Political science.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 1 citation. Notable citing venues include British Art Studies. They come from 2 countries, led by Canada and the United Kingdom.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It is recorded in 4 library collections. Its subject matter aligns with Reduced inequalities among the Sustainable Development Goals.</p>",
